00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
germany is bracing for a much tougher  pandemic lockdown set to begin in the  coming days  a soft lockdown imposed in early  november failed to cut infection rates  now the country faces hard choices as it  goes into  the holiday season let's go live to  german chancellor angela merkel's press  conference  she's just had a meeting with german  state leaders and is expected to  announce  an even tougher lockdown a surge in the  number of coronavirus deaths  has prompted her and the government to  take action let's listen  this is because the measures that we put  into place on the 2nd of november  have not been sufficient  for a while we were able to stop the  exponential growth  and had a plateau movement but now we  are seeing  a new rise in infections and exponential  growth once again  and what that means is that  many people are dying you'll have been  following the statistics i'm sure  and we also know that we are  close to exceeding the response capacity  of our public health  systems and our aim was always to  prevent  this and this is why  we must act and we must act fast and the  result  are the decisions that we made today the  aim  remains being able to trace  contacts once again so that means we  need an incidence  rate of 50 cases per 100 000 inhabitants  in a seven day period  and below now all of this will  impact on our holiday season as we are  well aware but we must act  and we will act  we have decided altogether that the  ordinances of the federal states will be  in place until the 10th of january  for now but the aim remains  to bring the incidence rate down  so what happens from early january  cannot be predicted now it will depend  on the results that we achieve with this  so we remain with our personal  contacts such that we can meet friends  and family members but a maximum of five  people  from two households at once  and this is only from the 24th until the  26th of december there will be an  exception  but not on new year's and not on new  year's eve  and so this means that above and beyond  your own household you  can invite for other people  in the holiday period from your closest  friends and families  your partners  direct relations so your parents  and your children and siblings  but we would like to appeal to all  citizens  if you're inviting other households over  for christmas  or other holidays please reduce your  contacts for  seven days before you do that so to have  a  protection week and then  from new year's afternoons there  will be no changes but from wednesday  the 16th of december we will be closing  retail apart from  essential goods retail  primarily food stores will not be  expanded and we are also putting a ban  on fireworks ahead of new year's eve and  there'll be an ordinance in place to  make this law  there will also be a ban on body care  services hairdressers beauty salons etc  schools will also be  limited and daycare centers as well  so that will mean that children are to  be looked  after at home wherever possible and from  the 16th of december so that's from  wednesday schools will be  closed certainly the school children no  longer have to go to school there will  be emergency care  in place for some children  and distance learning will also be  offered  the senior years of high school  might be dealt with differently and  daycare  will be run just the same as schools in  this regard we  are appealing to employers  to offer home office options  wherever possible from the 16th of  december until the 10th  of june  in terms of takeaway and delivery food  from restaurants this will continue to  be possible  but you are no longer allowed to eat  your takeaway  near or at the restaurant you will know  that in  recent days and weeks we have  again and again had a situation in which  there have been groups of people meeting  just  outside of cafes and restaurants  and they have been able to eat their  food just outside it  religious services will only be possible  under  strict constraints and we will be  speaking  with the churches and other  religious institutions we will be  focusing as well  on senior citizens homes  and homes for the very elderly there  will be mobile care services as well and  they will be getting  rapid tests as well we would  ask you to refrain from traveling abroad  if not absolutely necessary and the  quarantine  regulations will remain in place there  will be  economic support and the minister will  say more about that in a moment and  we've put together  a package of measures as well  which ensures that people are  compensated for the difficulties they'll  be experiencing  in their livelihood we are calling on  everyone to reduce  their contacts because wherever they can  and i want to thank  everyone in germany who has adhered to  these rules and regulations which you  have done to a large extent and i'd like  to urgently appeal to you  in the next days and weeks to avoid  contacts that aren't  absolutely necessary and by doing so to  contributing to  not exceeding the response capacity of  our public health systems and  those who work in hospitals the  physicians the care  geriatric care is the nurses i want to  thank all of you  because for you this is going to be a  very difficult holiday  season and we are  putting these efforts in place to  support you as well as  helping everyone stay well thank you  very much  [Music]  days and weeks there has been a process  of reaching an agreement between the  federal states and the national  government  and as the chancellor has just said  these  are tough measures for  nearly everyone they're tough for  families they're tough  for school children they're tough for  retail  and for many companies for the cultural  sector who still have no idea of  how things can proceed from here this is  a comprehensive  decision that we have agreed on  for myself i would just like to say a  bit about  my take on the situation  and to look back over the last few  months because in recent  days i've read again and again why now  why not a harder lockdown why can't  politicians agree on this that or the  other thing  if you look at what's been happening  since february and in march  in all of the federal states of germany  we have to say that we have responded  quickly  all of the state premiers have we have  restricted things we have closed things  from one day to the next  things that everyone took for granted  was suddenly not possible anymore  and we okay well angela merkel has been  leading with the 16 state leaders that  meeting has uh  ended we go live now to our political  correspondent hans brunt who is standing  by  hunts a lot to digest there what did you  make of it  well um there was at the moment as far  as i can see no surprise and what angela  mackel and her colleagues have now  announced or are busy announcing at the  moment in the chancellery that you see  behind me  the restrictions that had been agreed on  in a discussion paper  were it seems passed without too much  discussion  that's unusual for this kind of meeting  in the past these meetings since uh  sometime around october  have been very acrimonious and have  taken many many hours  for agreement to be reached so today  they have decided that there will be a  lockdown from  the 16th of december in other words this  coming wednesday  that retail shops will then be closed  except those shops  that sell essential goods that other  institutions such as schools will be  sent into  home schooling into distance learning  that companies are encouraged to give  their  employees off from that time across the  christmas period  or to also allow them to work at home  also closed will be hairdressers and  other  shops or other services that involve  very direct personal contact and they  have also imposed  a ban on the consumption of alcohol in  public spaces  and the use of fireworks around new year  so that's a whole gamut to try and  restrict the number of people that  gather  in public in private there will be a  restriction on five people  from two households that are allowed to  meet around christmas time that is  going to be uh loosened slightly it will  be five people but it does not need to  be only two households  yeah hence the wider holiday season will  change significantly this year from the  16th those changes come in  um another point up for discussion is  how that will affect  business merkel and state leaders also  discussed i believe compensation  yes indeed compensation was a central  part of this agreement that has now been  reached between the central government  and the  16 regional states and one is talking  about uh  an expense of somewhere around 10 or 12  billion euros every month in order to  compensate all the businesses  and all the and um  all the people who work for work for  themselves who work independently who  also can be compensated  um this amount of money has already been  spent in the last couple of months and  there has been some dispute between  central government  and the regions as to who is going to  carry uh  what part of that load so far it's been  central government that has paid most of  the money and there has been some  dissatisfaction amongst politicians here  in berlin  that the regions are not taking enough  share for themselves  at the moment it continues to be the  case that it is central government that  will pay  most of these 12 10 to 12 billion euros  every month  how exactly is going to be allocated is  this little a bit open yet  because until now the compensation that  has been paid in the last couple of  months has in some cases been too  generous  some restaurants for instance have been  doing better under lockdown than they  would have if they had been running  the details many details to follow hans  for your input thank you very much dwa  political correspondent hans brunt  you

